{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run the inventory web application on node2, listening on port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"node2 has active, enabled nginx bound to 10.100.16.11:8080. Direct HTTP checks returned the inventory HTML/API with backend identity node2, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-604f94f03ff546ba","cmd-9b26466911614b02","cmd-a3f5f6c795cf4497","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Run the inventory web application on node3, listening on port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"node3 has active, enabled nginx bound to 10.100.16.12:8080. Direct HTTP checks returned the inventory HTML/API with backend identity node3, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-05510a2a508b49bd","cmd-dfbbe585e7664846","cmd-6af667937af24007","global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Configure node1 to load-balance incoming HTTP requests on port 80 across both node2 and node3.","status":"satisfied","summary":"HAProxy is active and enabled on node1 at 10.100.16.10:80. Repeated requests from node1 and a separate managed client alternated between node2 and node3, and this behavior remained healthy after all restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d3c9dd33b127456f","cmd-7a44edfb6ead4336","cmd-f1582d05b50241f4","cmd-36297e41e89e47ef","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 before and after execution. HAProxy and nginx were installed from the RHEL AppStream repositories as Red Hat packages.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:before_prepare:node2:platform","global:before_prepare:node3:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node3:platform","cmd-848d4a96aaa84f0e","cmd-4f487ad4fdfb4874","cmd-13639f11a3af4ac3"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.95,"summary":"Retained mutations—vendor packages, application/configuration files, firewall and SELinux settings, enabled services, package-created service accounts, and rollback copies—have clear task or recovery roles. The only unnecessary mutations were cmd-ecaa6e10a5a842e9 on node2 and cmd-65487e42b3434ffb on node3: both wrote through nginx's packaged index symlink and altered /usr/share/testpage/index.html. They were fully reverted before service activation by package reinstalls and cleanup in cmd-b4cfcbe761884f18 and cmd-0e8640221c5344e2. Final verification shows healthy package state, no failed services, and no task temporary-file residue. The mandatory restart protocol was complete for every node: healthy pre-state and boot identity, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service/data and load-balancer state; fixed lifecycle boot observations corroborate the results. The deduction reflects the two low-risk, fully repaired mistaken edits.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ecaa6e10a5a842e9","cmd-65487e42b3434ffb","cmd-b4cfcbe761884f18","cmd-0e8640221c5344e2","cmd-36297e41e89e47ef","cmd-a3f5f6c795cf4497","cmd-6af667937af24007","cmd-2bdd10f8d9384bd5","cmd-c4d521e899bb45ac","cmd-f1582d05b50241f4","cmd-70411e840338447b","cmd-92b16cc9ab3a4a33","cmd-9b26466911614b02","cmd-de283d0e995048e6","cmd-a26432142a394279","cmd-bf7eb7dbff084990","cmd-dfbbe585e7664846","cmd-d958a9959fe44efb","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All four material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The independent provider-wide restart protocol is also complete and coherent across all three nodes, with lifecycle snapshots confirming the post-restart boot identities. Operational hygiene was strong apart from two package-file edits that were detected and fully restored.","limitations":[]}
